WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.269
-The president's use
of a Sharpie

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.338
to doctor an official
hurricane forecast

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.239
is now an actual scandal

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:10.376
that has prompted multiple
official investigations.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.578
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:14.080
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.416 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.319
-So you remember how
like two weeks ago,

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.487
there was this whole thing
where a dangerous hurricane

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.689
named Dorian was headed toward
the United States,

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:26.159
and so the president, you know,
the guy whose job it is

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.895
to protect Americans,
tweeted out that Alabama

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.597
will most likely be hit
much harder than anticipated.

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:33.932
And then some people in Alabama
started to freak out.

00:00:33.932 --> 00:00:35.768
So then the National
Weather Service had to be like,

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:38.571
"No, Alabama will not see
any impacts from Dorian."

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.939
And instead of just
letting it go,

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.375
the president took out a big map
in the oval office

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.444
and drew a little circle on it
with a Sharpie

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:47.813
to include Alabama and make it
look like he was right?

00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:50.449
You know, like he was
accepting one of those

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:52.852
giant novelty checks
for a thousand dollars,

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.854
but then wrote in a bunch
of zeros and went,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.223
[ As Trump ] "Wow, you're
giving me a billion dollars?

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.626
Too generous, but I accept.
No takebacks."

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.827
[ Normal voice ]
You remember that whole thing?

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:01.961
It was fun.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:05.531
Well, anyway, after like
a full week of coverage,

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:08.401
we all thought it was over.
We wanted to let it go.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.803
The White House
wanted to let it go.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.539
Even the PR Department
at the Sharpie company

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:14.873
was probably like,

00:01:14.873 --> 00:01:18.211
"Okay, maybe there is such
a thing as bad publicity."

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.345
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.747
And I'm sure Alabama
wanted to let it go,

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:23.550
because for a week
they were all, like,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.217
"Are we going to get hit
by a hurricane or not?

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:27.386
Because I've been sleeping
on a cot

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:29.955
in a high school gymnasium
for seven days."

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.357
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:33.893
Well, guess what --

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.561
It's not over. That's right.

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:38.431
The whole insane Sharpie thing
is still going.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.167
First, we found out
earlier this week that staff

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.969
at the National Oceanic
and Atmospheric Administration

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:45.538
were instructed
not to contradict

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.506
the president's Sharpie
hurricane forecast.

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:50.309
And then we found out that
the Secretary of Commerce,

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:52.979
Wilbur Ross,
threatened firings at NOAA

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.380
after Trump's Dorian tweets.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.616
That's right, Wilbur Ross,
the guy who once tried

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.552
to defend Trump's tariffs
on steel and aluminum

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:03.956
by holding up a beer and can
of soup in a live TV interview,

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.725
threatened to fire
actual scientists

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.126
for contradicting the president.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:10.496
Look at this. He looks like
he's bringing hurricane supplies

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.231
to Alabama.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:15.268
[ Higher-pitched voice ]
I -- I don't have water,

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:18.604
but how about a soup and beer
party?

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:21.207
[ Normal voice ] So Wilbur Ross
threatened to fire scientists

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.442
for issuing accurate
weather forecasts

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.611
that contradicted
the president's stupid tweets.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:28.848
But, hey, it's not like
Wilbur Ross has ever, himself,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.417
committed an actual fireable
offense, right?

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:34.854
-A federal judge has taken
the extraordinary step

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.855
in ruling that
Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross

00:02:36.855 --> 00:02:39.492
acted in bad faith
and broke several laws

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.828
when he asked a citizenship
question to the 2020 census.

00:02:42.828 --> 00:02:45.431
-Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross
held in contempt.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.767
Now this battle is all about
Ross hiding evidence

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.868
that might show whether
Republicans

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.672
changed the 2020 census
to discriminate

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.707
and help their own party,
the GOP.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.942
-The president's
Commerce Secretary, Wilbur Ross,

00:02:56.942 --> 00:02:58.978
stands accused
of misappropriating

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:03.349
or outright stealing as much
as $120 million

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.484
from former investors
and business partners.

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:07.887
That's according to a new
investigation from "Forbes."

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:11.591
-We all know Wilbur Ross
had problems before this.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.592
Aides have been saying from
the beginning

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:15.694
he regularly falls asleep
in meetings.

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:18.664
-Ross was famously caught
sleeping during Trump's speech

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:20.432
to Muslim leaders
in Saudi Arabia

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:22.201
back in May of 2017.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:23.635
-And on top of all that,

00:03:23.635 --> 00:03:26.072
two former colleagues remember
the Commerce Secretary

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:29.909
taking handfuls of Sweet'N Low
packets from a nearby restaurant

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:33.646
so he didn't have to go out
and buy some for himself.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.781
So he's an alleged criminal

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:37.416
who took Sweet'N Low from
restaurants

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:38.851
and falls asleep in meetings.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.387
He's like a character
from a Clint Eastwood movie

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.723
where a bunch of old guys
plan a bank heist.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.425
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.559
[ Gruff voice ]
You guys grab the money,

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.427
I'll grab the soup and beer.

00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:49.895
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:53.633
[ Normal voice ] Also, just let
it sink in that Wilbur Ross

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:56.335
is a billionaire
who steals Sweet'N Low,

00:03:56.335 --> 00:04:01.040
which is in no way sweet,
but it's plenty [bleep] low.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.576
I mean, how about instead
of a citizenship question,

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.011
the census asks,
"Are you a billionaire

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:07.513
who steals Sweet'N Low?"

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:10.383
And if you answer yes,
we shoot you into space.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.617
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:13.552
So that was all stuff
that happened this week.

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:15.788
And as a result, Democrats
called on Ross to resign

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.457
and NOAA's Chief Scientist

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:18.958
said he would investigate
what happened.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.627
Now, you think that would be
the end of it,

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:23.029
but no, this insane story
is still a thing.

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:25.564
In fact, it's even more
of a thing now

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:28.501
because yesterday, we found out
that the White House itself

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:32.104
was directly involved in efforts
to pressure officials at NOAA

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:35.041
to side with the president
over their own scientists.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.375
-"The New York Times" reports

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.112
that acting White House
Chief of Staff Mick Mulvaney

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.314
told commerce secretary
Wilbur Ross

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:44.417
to have the National Oceanic
and Atmospheric Administration

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:48.353
NOAA, publicly disavow
this tweet that was sent

00:04:48.353 --> 00:04:52.358
by the National Weather Service
office in Birmingham, Alabama,

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:55.494
which said the state would not
feel the effects of the storm.

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:57.630
A senior administration official
told the "Times"

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.198
Mulvaney wanted to correct
the record

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:03.936
because he felt the Birmingham
tweet went too far.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:07.407
National Weather Service tweet
went too far.

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:09.976
One that actually
forecasts the weather.

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:11.210
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.912
-Think about how insane this is.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.214
Two of the most senior officials
in our government

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:18.117
called up a scientific agency
and threatened to fire them

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.286
unless they changed
their forecast

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:23.188
about a dangerous hurricane
just so they could pretend

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:25.291
the president was right
when he accidentally said

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:28.294
a state that was not in the
Hurricane's path would get hit.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.363
I mean, what's next,
are they going to make Melania

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:33.366
change her name to Melanie to
justify Trump's typo tweet?

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:34.733
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:37.236
I'm shocked Trump
didn't just go all the way

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:40.739
and make Congress pass
a disaster aid bill for Alabama.

00:05:40.739 --> 00:05:41.808
[ As Trump ]
I'm here in Montgomery

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:44.043
to help rebuild
from the hurricane.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.344
And in the meantime,

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:48.447
we'll be moving all these people
into temporary shelters.

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:49.849
[ Normal voice ]
But my house is fine.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:51.650
[ As Trump ]
No, your house was destroyed.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.152
Here, look at this photo.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:55.454
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:59.091
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:01.394
[ Normal voice ] So...

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:05.564
this insane, dumb thing
the president did

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:07.399
that we all desperately
wanted to move on from

00:06:07.399 --> 00:06:08.200
will not go away.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.735
In fact, and this is real,

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:11.136
this whole thing has now
triggered

00:06:11.136 --> 00:06:13.105
multiple official
investigations.

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:15.774
NOAA's Chief Scientist
has said he would investigate

00:06:15.774 --> 00:06:18.644
why the agency backed Trump
over its experts on Dorian.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.480
The Commerce Department
Inspector General

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.481
has opened an investigation,
and on Wednesday,

00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:24.784
a Democrat-controlled
House Science Committee

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:26.085
kicked off its own inquiry.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.486
This all started with a Sharpie.

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:30.022
If the pen is mightier
than the sword,

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:31.590
the Sharpie
is a long-range missile.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.526
I mean, this is
an actual scandal now.

00:06:34.526 --> 00:06:36.328
There are multiple
investigations.

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:39.264
That means there's a chance,
which would be awesome,

00:06:39.264 --> 00:06:42.101
we could have meteorologists
testifying before Congress.

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:43.502
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:45.571
[ Southern accent ] Please state
your name for the record.

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.807
[ Normal voice ]
Uh, my name is Breeze Thunder.

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:50.143
[ Southern accent ]
And Mr. Thunder,

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:52.244
where did the president
tell you to lie?

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:55.347
[ Normal voice ] Well, first,
the lies began over here,

00:06:55.347 --> 00:06:58.885
but then they eventually picked
up speed and moved down here.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.652
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.652 --> 00:07:05.791
[ Southern accent ]
Also, And remember,

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:08.727
remember, that you are
under oath.

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:14.233
Mr. Thunder, is dew point
an actual thing?

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:15.368
[ Normal voice ] No, it is not.

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.602
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.236
Seriously, this is now
officially the craziest

00:07:18.236 --> 00:07:21.374
weather-related scandal America
has seen since this one.

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:23.275
-Right now dew points in the 20s

00:07:23.275 --> 00:07:26.011
and near 30 degrees
across central Mississippi.

00:07:26.011 --> 00:07:27.345
Well, hey, there.

00:07:27.345 --> 00:07:29.849
-I don't know what's going on,
but Zane doesn't know.

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:31.817
[ Laughter ]
Are you sure?

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:34.820
Are you crazy sure?
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:39.425
Well, we've got a little bit
of interesting things

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:40.860
going on right now.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.595
Take a look at what's
going on right now.

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:44.163
You want to point out
the weather right now?

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:47.466
-Yeah, there are farts
everywhere and toots.

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:49.101
I don't even know. It's crazy.

00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:50.836
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:52.738
-You laugh. You laugh.

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:54.173
Trump just made that kid

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.676
Director of
the National Weather Service.

00:07:56.676 --> 00:08:00.045
[ As Trump ] I'm hearing Alabama
is about to get hit very hard

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:02.581
with farts and toots.
It's scary.

00:08:02.581 --> 00:08:04.583
But the National Guard
will be ringing --

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:07.018
will be bringing matches
and Glade PlugIns

00:08:07.018 --> 00:08:09.188
to the affected areas.

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:11.456
[ Normal voice ] Yesterday Trump
was asked in the oval office

00:08:11.456 --> 00:08:13.859
about the report that
his Chief of Staff

00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:16.228
instructed NOAA to disavow
their own scientists

00:08:16.228 --> 00:08:17.329
and side with Trump,

00:08:17.329 --> 00:08:19.565
and Trump pretended
that he personally

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:20.766
had nothing to do with it.

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:24.103
-Did you tell
your Chief of Staff to have NOAA

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:27.139
disavow those forecasters
to who said that Alabama

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:29.208
was not --
-No, I never did that.

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:30.376
I never did that.

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:33.512
That's a whole hoax
by the fake news media

00:08:33.512 --> 00:08:35.047
when they talk about
the hurricane

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:38.284
and when they talk about Florida
and they talk about Alabama.

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:39.751
That stuff, just fake news.

00:08:39.751 --> 00:08:42.755
It was -- right from the
beginning, it was a fake story.

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:45.124
-He just covers lies
with more lies.

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:46.559
I'm surprised he didn't say...

00:08:46.559 --> 00:08:48.761
[ As Trump ] This is a really
hard week for me because --

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:49.862
and I didn't want to say this,

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:52.297
but I was also
hit by the hurricane.

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:54.566
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:54.566 --> 00:08:56.535
[ Normal voice ] So Trump
denied that he personally

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:59.505
ordered his aides to intervene
and tell a scientific agency

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:01.007
to lie about
a dangerous hurricane

00:09:01.007 --> 00:09:03.676
in order to justify
an embarrassing tweet

00:09:03.676 --> 00:09:05.477
and a map he doctored
with a Sharpie.

00:09:05.477 --> 00:09:07.513
Well, you'll never guess
what happened next.

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:09.948
On Wednesday, the news broke
that, yes,

00:09:09.948 --> 00:09:12.918
it was, in fact, Trump who
ordered the Sharpie cover-up.

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:15.354
-"New York Times" today
and "The Washington Post"

00:09:15.354 --> 00:09:18.224
revealed that the White House
and Donald Trump, himself,

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:20.559
were behind threats against
weather forecasters

00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:23.295
who, wait for it --
forecasted the weather.

00:09:23.295 --> 00:09:26.465
"The Washington Post" adds
that the president, himself,

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:28.834
was behind the threats
to the weather forecasters.

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:30.502
President Trump told his staff

00:09:30.502 --> 00:09:32.605
that NOAA needed to deal
with the tweet

00:09:32.605 --> 00:09:34.773
that seemed to contradict
his statement

00:09:34.773 --> 00:09:38.176
that hurricane Dorian posed
a significant threat to Alabama.

00:09:38.176 --> 00:09:40.145
-Of course,
it was Trump who ordered it.

00:09:40.145 --> 00:09:43.048
Trump orders his aides to lie
all the time.

00:09:43.048 --> 00:09:45.851
He doesn't even let Mulvaney
cough in his presence

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:47.119
without permission.

00:09:47.119 --> 00:09:49.855
-Trump, interrupting
his interview with ABC News,

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:52.457
to scold his Chief of Staff,
Mick Mulvaney,

00:09:52.457 --> 00:09:54.460
for coughing
while he was speaking.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:55.694
-But at some point,
I hope they get it...

00:09:55.694 --> 00:09:57.896
-[ Coughs ]
...because it's a fantastic

00:09:57.896 --> 00:09:59.265
financial statement.

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:02.167
It's a fantastic financial
statement.

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:03.502
And -- Let's do that over.

00:10:03.502 --> 00:10:05.638
He's coughing in the middle
of my answer.

00:10:05.638 --> 00:10:07.472
-Yeah, okay.
-I don't like that, you know?

00:10:07.472 --> 00:10:09.675
-Your Chief of Staff --
-If you're going to cough,

00:10:09.675 --> 00:10:11.577
please leave the room.
-We should get a shot of --

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:14.045
and I'll come over here.
-Just can't --

00:10:14.045 --> 00:10:16.382
You just can't do that.
-Okay.

00:10:16.382 --> 00:10:18.417
-Sorry, Mr. Trump.

00:10:18.417 --> 00:10:20.586
-Hey, you leave him alone.

00:10:20.586 --> 00:10:22.755
He was probably coughing
from all the dust

00:10:22.755 --> 00:10:25.590
kicked up by that hurricane.

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:27.626
At least we knew it wasn't
Wilbur Ross who was coughing,

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:29.361
because he was probably
sound asleep.

00:10:29.361 --> 00:10:32.898
He'd, uh -- He'd been up all
night stealing Sweet'N Low.

00:10:32.898 --> 00:10:34.099
[ Laughter ]

